#83001
"A Subterranean Stream"
"A powerful stream of water flows from the east along a crevice in the floor,
emptying out abruptly across a series of descending small waterfalls to the
west.  The air within the cavern feels thick with humidity, contrasting the
biting wind which blows in from the east - it's eerie sounds bouncing along
the corridor.  The somewhat melodic sound of water rippling down the small
waterfalls is distracting.  The sharp edges of each level seem unnatural and
somewhat resemble a rugged stairwell.
"
""
