"Hewn Granite Cavern"
"Water pools at the base of what appears to be a flight of stairs leading
upward.  The water flows rapidly down the apparent stairwell then runs from
the overflowing puddle across the floor to the west.  The stones appear to
have been worn smooth by the constant flow of water.  The walls appear to be
nothing more than massive granite blocks.  Above, slabs of stone seal off
whatever is beyond, whether sky, soil, or stream.
"
